35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The call-back trial reduced readmissions by a fifth, but the shared nursing round lost a third of visits. We must verify if the new program can sustain this fragile operational reality.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The booking system erases unstructured work. Rooms and parking saturate by eleven. The shuttle misses fifteen villages. This infrastructure cannot absorb another variable load.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The data agreements took fourteen months to sign. The jointly run clinic collapsed because neither department owned the rota. We are building on sand, not stone.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Nine unfilled posts and rising agency costs! But midwifery has slack. We must pick a program that uses the spare hands, not the exhausted ones!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The ledger is down a quarter, and off-site work earns nothing. We must choose a program that generates on-site revenue to sustain itself.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, your infrastructure constraints are critical. If the shuttle misses villages, outreach fails. We need a program that operates within existing, reliable boundaries.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, precisely. The system only counts what fits a slot. We must select a program that operates within the existing, rigid boundaries, not one that demands new infrastructure.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, boundaries are necessary, but ownership is fatal. If the arrangement rests on an outside body that never signed up, it will fracture. We need internal control.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I agree! We need internal control. But we also need to use the midwifery slack! Let’s pick a program that fits our current staffing reality.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, the midwifery slack is a lifeline. But we must ensure the program stays on-site to capture the tariffs. Off-site work is a financial void.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, on-site revenue is vital, but my data shows the call-back trial only worked while actively staffed. We need a program with sustainable, internal ownership, not a fragile trial.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, sustainable ownership is vital, but only if the physical space exists. My data shows the car park and rooms are already saturated. We must choose a program that fits within these rigid, existing limits.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, space is a constraint, but ownership is the fracture point. We must avoid any model dependent on external bodies or shared rotas that have already failed.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I agree! We must avoid external dependencies. But we also need to use the midwifery slack! Let’s pick a program that fits our current staffing reality.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, ownership is the root. I concur. We must select a program that is internally owned, on-site, and leverages the midwifery slack to ensure financial and operational stability.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, I concur. We need a program that is internally owned, on-site, and leverages the midwifery slack. This ensures the impact is real, not just another buried initiative.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
